"""Bind the actual dependency commands, four client builds, media and retained history."""
from datetime import datetime, timezone
import hashlib
import importlib.util
import json
from pathlib import Path
import socket
import subprocess
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
import zipfile
from PIL import Image

APP = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
ROOT = APP.parent
E = ROOT / 'docs/quality/evidence/task-dependencies'
REF = 'e45c347a31cc7496b77585dc5328bcfdec92ec6d'


def read(path):
    return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))


def sha(path):
    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def digest(names, content=None):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    for name in names:
        h.update(name.encode() + b'\0' + (content(name) if content else (APP / name).read_bytes()) + b'\0')
    return h.hexdigest()


def module(filename):
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('dependency_' + filename.replace('.', '_'), APP / 'scripts' / filename)
    value = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(value)
    return value


def main():
    checks = []

    def check(name, passed):
        checks.append({'name': name, 'passed': bool(passed)})

    backend = read(E / 'result.json')
    backend_sha = module('verify_backend_batches.py').digest()
    check('Fresh full native backend:162 top-level tests,1080 results,9 batches and stable complete sources',
        backend['passed'] and backend['source_sha256'] == backend_sha and backend['source_unchanged_during_tests']
        and backend['all_discovered_tests_executed'] and backend['discovered_top_level_tests'] == 162
        and backend['batch_count'] == 9 and len(backend['checks']) == 1080 and all(v['Action'] == 'pass' for v in backend['checks']))
    cases = [c for c in backend['checks'] if c.get('Test', '').startswith('TestAgentTaskDependencies')]
    check('Actual HTTP/PostgreSQL/MCP dependency suite has22 nested cases, including authority, replay, cycle and receipt rollback',
        len(cases) == 23 and all(c['Action'] == 'pass' for c in cases))
    migrations = sorted((APP / 'backend/migrations').glob('*.sql'))
    check('Additive migration74 preserves exact published bytes of all73 previous migrations',
        len(migrations) == 74 and migrations[-1].name == '0074_agent_task_dependencies.sql'
        and all(subprocess.check_output(['git', 'show', REF + ':' + p.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()], cwd=ROOT) == p.read_bytes() for p in migrations[:-1]))
    api_file = ROOT / 'docs/development/openapi.json'
    api = read(api_file)
    check('Both current OpenAPI copies agree:284 paths,352 operations,619 schemas and the exact dependency tool',
        api_file.read_bytes() == (APP / 'backend/internal/contract/openapi.json').read_bytes()
        and len(api['paths']) == 284 and len(api['components']['schemas']) == 619
        and sum(k in ('get','post','put','patch','delete','head','options','trace') for p in api['paths'].values() for k in p) == 352
        and all('update_task_dependency' in api['components']['schemas'][s]['properties']['tool']['enum'] for s in ('AgentMutationInput','AgentMutationView')))
    runtime, web = read(E / 'runtime-build.json'), read(E / 'web-build.json')
    check('Fresh49 runtime tests and build bind current runtime and Skill bytes',
        runtime['status'] == 'passed' and runtime['source_sha256'] == module('verify_agent_runtime.py').digest()[0]
        and runtime['tests']['tests'] == runtime['tests']['pass'] == 49
        and all(runtime['tests'][k] == 0 for k in ('fail','skipped','cancelled')))
    check('Fresh120 Web tests and production bundle bind every declared current source byte',
        web['passed'] and web['source_unchanged_during_run'] and web['source_sha256'] == digest(web['sources'])
        and web['tests']['numPassedTests'] == 120 and web['tests']['numFailedTests'] == 0)
    linux = read(E / 'linux-build.json')
    check('Fresh Linux compilation matches current complete backend; artifact was not executed or deployed',
        linux['passed'] and linux['source_sha256'] == linux['source_after_sha256'] == backend_sha
        and not linux['artifact_executed'] and not linux['deployed'])
    mobile = read(E / 'mobile-build.json')
    check('Fresh212 mobile tests, types and both actual mini-program builds bind complete unchanged declared sources',
        mobile['passed'] and mobile['source_unchanged_during_run'] and mobile['source_sha256'] == module('verify_mobile.py').digest()[0]
        and mobile['tests']['tests'] == mobile['tests']['pass'] == 212 and mobile['tests']['suites'] == 2
        and all(mobile['tests'][k] == 0 for k in ('fail','skipped','cancelled'))
        and len(mobile['commands']) == 4 and all(c['exit_code'] == 0 for c in mobile['commands']))
    pages = [read(APP / ('mobile/dist/' + target + '/app.json'))['pages'] for target in ('weapp','tt')]
    check('WeChat and Douyin each register the same18 pages including the secretary',
        pages[0] == pages[1] and len(pages[0]) == 18 and 'pages/secretary/index' in pages[0])
    android, inspection, unit = [read(E / n) for n in ('build.json','apk-inspection.json','android-test-scope.json')]
    check('Current native Android APK binds actual bundle/source bytes and all18 artifact checks; no device or release claim',
        android['passed'] and android['source_unchanged_during_build'] and android['source_sha256'] == module('build_android.py').sources()[0]
        and sha(APP / android['artifacts']['apk']['path']) == android['artifacts']['apk']['sha256'] == inspection['apk_sha256']
        and inspection['passed'] and len(inspection['checks']) == 18 and all(c['passed'] for c in inspection['checks'])
        and not any(android[k] for k in ('device_executed','production_release','virtualization_used','emulator_started')))
    native_graph = [n.replace('\\', '/') for n in read(APP / '.local/android/index.android.map')['sources']]
    check('Actual APK business graph includes the new secretary dependency form and shared exact-input validation',
        all(any(n.endswith(suffix) for n in native_graph) for suffix in ('/mobile/src/pages/secretary/task-dependency.tsx','/packages/contracts/src/task-dependency.ts')))
    xml = sorted((E / 'android-unit-results').glob('TEST-*.xml'))
    suites = [ET.parse(p).getroot() for p in xml]
    check('All26 JVM results retain exact XML/task bytes and explicitly disclose Gradle cache reuse',
        unit['passed'] and unit['tests'] == 26 and unit['native_log_sha256'] == sha(E / 'native-build.log')
        and unit['freezer_sha256'] == sha(APP / 'scripts/freeze_task_dependencies_evidence.py')
        and len(xml) == 4 and sum(int(s.attrib['tests']) for s in suites) == 26
        and all(int(s.attrib[k]) == 0 for s in suites for k in ('failures','errors','skipped'))
        and all(unit['xml_sha256'][p.name] == sha(p) for p in xml)
        and unit['new_test_execution'] != unit['gradle_cached'] and not unit['device_executed'])
    full_sha = module('task_dependencies_sources.py').digest()
    for client in ('web','mobile'):
        b = E.parent / ('task-dependencies-' + client)
        browser, manifest, capture = [read(b / n) for n in ('result.json','source-manifest.json','capture.json')]
        check(client + ': five actual dependency journeys, three widths and complete owned cleanup bind stable full sources',
            browser['passed'] and len(browser['checks']) == 5 and len(capture['layouts']) == 3
            and browser['source_sha256'] == browser['source_after_sha256'] == manifest['sha256'] == digest(manifest['files'])
            and browser['build_source_sha256'] == browser['build_source_after_sha256'] == full_sha
            and browser['source_unchanged'] and browser['build_source_unchanged']
            and browser['native_fixture_exit_code'] == 0 and browser['isolated_database_cleanup_passed']
            and browser['owned_browser_closed'] and browser['owned_review_server_stopped'] and browser['browser_contexts_closed'] == 1
            and not browser['console_errors'] and not browser['server_errors']
            and all(v['document'] <= v['width'] + 2 for v in capture['layouts']))
    media = read(E / 'media.json')
    media_valid = media['passed'] and media['encoder_script_sha256'] == sha(APP / 'scripts/encode_task_dependencies_media.py') and len(media['recordings']) == 2
    for r in media['recordings']:
        result = read(E.parent / ('task-dependencies-' + r['client']) / 'result.json')
        media_valid = media_valid and r['source_sha256'] == result['source_sha256'] and r['build_source_sha256'] == full_sha
        media_valid = media_valid and r['capture_manifest_sha256'] == sha(ROOT / r['capture_manifest']) and r['capture_frame_count'] > 5
        media_valid = media_valid and len(r['artifacts']) == 2 and all(sha(ROOT / a['file']) == a['sha256'] and (ROOT / a['file']).stat().st_size == a['bytes'] for a in r['artifacts'])
        with Image.open(next(ROOT / a['file'] for a in r['artifacts'] if a['file'].endswith('.gif'))) as picture:
            duration = 0
            for index in range(picture.n_frames):
                picture.seek(index)
                duration += picture.info.get('duration', 0)
            media_valid = media_valid and picture.n_frames > 1 and abs(duration * r['gif_speed_multiplier'] - r['capture_duration_ms']) < 800
    check('Two actual pixel captures bind four MP4/GIF artifacts, frame manifests, encoder and bounded animation timing', media_valid)
    visual = read(E / 'visual-review.json')
    check('Actual visual review binds all eight screenshots and both GIF first/middle/last samples',
        visual['passed'] and len(visual['files']) == 10 and all(sha(ROOT / p['file']) == p['sha256'] for p in visual['files']))
    skills = [read(p) for p in sorted((APP / 'skills').glob('*/manifest.json'))]
    update = next(s for s in skills if s['skill_id'] == 'project-update')
    check('All eight Skills stay draft; project-update1.7.0 has17 allowed and15 completion tools',
        len(skills) == 8 and all(s['state'] == 'draft' for s in skills) and update['version'] == '1.7.0'
        and len(update['allowed_tools']) == 17 and len(update['completion_tools']) == 15
        and 'update_task_dependency' in update['allowed_tools'])
    dev = read(E / 'development-project-resources.json')
    check('Fresh development probes establish74 migrations, actual dependency guards, owned DB workers and zero disposable databases',
        dev['passed'] and dev['migration_count'] == 74 and dev['integrations_disabled'] and dev['all_eight_skills_draft']
        and dev['database']['disposable_test_databases'] == dev['database']['active_profiles'] == dev['database']['enabled_telegram_channels'] == 0
        and all(dev['ownership'].values()) and dev['report_worker_source_matches'] and dev['database']['report_guards'] == 4
        and dev['database']['dependency_tool_constraints'] == 3 and dev['database']['dependency_scope_constraint'] == 1
        and dev['database']['dependency_guards'] == 2 and dev['database']['dependency_actual_edge_function'])
    history = read(E / 'historical-90.json')
    check('Published90 complete startup/capture reconstruct from Git; all84 original evidence/media files remain unchanged',
        history == module('record_task_dependencies_history.py').reconstruct()
        and history['complete_startup_source']['reconstructed'] and len(history['preserved_evidence']) == 84
        and history['preserved_media_count'] == 8 and all(v['complete_capture_manifest_reconstructed'] for v in history['clients'].values()))
    publication = read(E / 'publication-before.json')
    check('All11 publication snapshots retain exact original published90 bytes',
        len(publication['files']) == 11 and all(sha(ROOT / f['snapshot']) == f['sha256']
            and (ROOT / f['snapshot']).read_bytes() == subprocess.check_output(['git','show',publication['commit'] + ':' + f['file']],cwd=ROOT) for f in publication['files']))
    audit = read(E.parent / 'dependency-hardening/dependency-audit.json')
    check('Original90 audit is reused for the unchanged exact lock; all86 findings and the open production security gate remain explicit',
        audit['package_lock_sha256'] == sha(APP / 'package-lock.json')
        and (APP / 'package-lock.json').read_bytes() == subprocess.check_output(['git','show',REF + ':app/package-lock.json'],cwd=ROOT)
        and audit['vulnerabilities']['total'] == 86 and audit['vulnerabilities']['critical'] == 0
        and audit['vulnerabilities']['high'] == 20 and not audit['production_security_gate_passed'])
    attempts_valid, attempts = True, []
    for p in sorted((E / 'attempts').glob('*/attempt.json')):
        a = read(p)
        attempts.append(p.parent.name)
        with zipfile.ZipFile(p.parent / 'sources.zip') as z:
            attempts_valid = attempts_valid and a['source_zip_sha256'] == sha(p.parent / 'sources.zip') and a['diagnostic_only']
            if 'startup_manifest' in a:
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and len(z.namelist()) == a['source_count']
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and digest(a['startup_manifest'],z.read) == a['complete_startup_source_sha256']
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and digest(a['source_manifest'],z.read) == a['capture_source_sha256']
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and a['owned_browser_closed'] and a['owned_review_server_stopped'] and a['isolated_database_cleanup_passed']
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and a['passed'] == read(p.parent / 'result.json')['passed']
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and (not a['passed'] or a['superseded'])
            elif 'complete_source_sha256' in a:
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and digest(a['source_manifest'],z.read) == a['complete_source_sha256']
                if a.get('superseded'):
                    attempts_valid = attempts_valid and a['passed'] and a['android_build_pass_claimed']
                    attempts_valid = attempts_valid and all(read(p.parent / n)['passed'] for n in ('mobile-build.json','build.json'))
                    attempts_valid = attempts_valid and all(read(p.parent / n)['passed'] for n in ('web-build.json','media.json') if (p.parent / n).exists())
                else:
                    attempts_valid = attempts_valid and not a['passed'] and not a['android_build_pass_claimed']
            else:
                attempts_valid = attempts_valid and digest(a['source_files'],lambda n: z.read('backend/' + n)) == a['backend_source_sha256'] and not a['passed']
    check('Every retained failed or explicitly superseded attempt preserves exact complete source bytes and its original status', attempts_valid and len(attempts) >= 6)
    with socket.socket() as probe:
        probe.settimeout(1)
        released = probe.connect_ex(('127.0.0.1',5189)) != 0
    check('Owned review port is released and private fixture removed', released and not (APP / '.local/business-browser-fixture.json').exists())
    gaps = (ROOT / 'docs/delivery/03-goal-gap-assessment.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
    check('All28 gap IDs and complete four-client scope remain explicit',
        all('GAP-' + str(i).zfill(2) in gaps for i in range(1,29)) and all(t in gaps for t in ('120GB','2TB','Android','微信','抖音')))
    report = {'passed': all(c['passed'] for c in checks), 'checked_at': datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),
        'checks': checks, 'backend_source_sha256': backend_sha, 'browser_source_sha256': full_sha,
        'mobile_source_sha256': mobile['source_sha256'], 'full_goal_complete': False,
        'attempts': attempts, 'reused_audit_group': 'dependency-hardening', 'audit_reexecuted': False,
        'verification_script_sha256': sha(Path(__file__)),
        'scope': 'Fresh native backend/Web/runtime/mobile/Linux/Android checks and actual synthetic UI pixels. Explicit JVM cache and old-lock audit reuse. No real model/device/cloud/TG/production acceptance.'}
    (E / 'final-source-check.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + '\n', encoding='utf-8')
    print(json.dumps({'passed': report['passed'], 'checks': len(checks), 'failed': [c['name'] for c in checks if not c['passed']]}))
    return 0 if report['passed'] else 1


if __name__ == '__main__':
    raise SystemExit(main())
